Role Summary



The Software Quality Engineer is responsible for software reliability, test automation and continuous quality improvement across the AI Platform. The role shall define and execute testing approaches covering both conventional software components and agentic AI capabilities, including functional, integration, security, performance and AI\-quality testing.



The Software Quality Engineer shall demonstrate proficiency in:



a) testing agentic AI and document\-processing solutions;



b) testing cloud\-native solutions deployed on AWS GCC;



c) testing secure APIs and enterprise integrations;



d) designing and implementing automated test frameworks and CI/CD quality gates;



e) testing systems handling legally sensitive and personal data; and



f) working in Agile and DevOps\-driven teams using risk\-based testing and fast feedback loops.



g) Experience testing on OutSystems Platform will be advantageous.



Responsibilities



* Collaborate with Business owner and business consultant to define clear and actionable user story acceptance criteria;
* Work with Backend Engineers to ensure automated test coverage and prevent bugs and defects in production;
* Analyse and decompose complex software systems to design holistic, risk\-based test strategies;
* Develop and maintain test automation frameworks using industry\-standard tools
* Design, implement, and execute comprehensive test suites covering functional, regression, exploratory, and performance testing;
* Take a risk\-based approach to test automation, prioritizing critical functionality for maximum impact;
* Perform time\-boxed exploratory testing to uncover edge cases and usability issues;
* Maintain a stable regression test suite integrated into QA nightly builds;
* Continuously refine smoke tests in the Development CI environment for early issue detection;
* Lead system integration testing with other system owners to validate cross\-system interactions;
* Oversee UAT, coordinating with stakeholders to ensure business requirements are met;
* Manage the defect lifecycle, test artifacts, and test repositories to ensure clear tracking and reporting;
* Drive continuous improvement in agile testing practices, tools, and methodologies;
* Take on a secondary role as an Application Performance Engineer or Application Security Engineer to expand testing coverage beyond functional aspects;
* Assist in product development where relevant; and
* Design agentic AI evaluation testing to cover output accuracy and agent\-level behaviour


